Hypothesis: The method mixes dimensions for unbound parameters and all parameters. It calls updateJacobian(), which fills the jacobian array using the estimator fields rows/cols established from unbound parameters only. But then getCovariances recomputes cols as problem.getAllParameters().length and iterates as if jacobian had rows * allParameters entries. When some parameters are bound, cols is too large, causing out-of-bounds indexing into jacobian and also producing the wrong covariance dimension. The fix is likely to use the unbound-parameter count (or estimator field cols / parameters.length) consistently.

